Sources of Rust crates with IRIX 6.5 (mips64-sgi-irix, N32) support, for
cargo to use in place of the crates.io releases ([patch.crates-io]) when
cross-building Rust programs for IRIX: libc, with an IRIX module describing
IRIX as the IRIX toolchain (clang with its IRIX header wrappers and builtins)
sees it, and the crates that pick their code by operating system (getrandom,
mio, parking_lot_core, socket2, libloading, rustix, errno, tokio), taught IRIX.
